      "title": "Poisson in each window is not yet independence",
      "html": "<figure class=\"volume7-explain\" id=\"visual-V48\" data-v7=\"V48\" lang=\"en\"><header><span>V48</span><h3>Poisson in each window is not yet independence</h3></header><p>Each window has the same count law. Which joint events change when we connect the inputs?</p><div class=\"v7-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-mode=\"independent\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Two independent Poisson counts</button><button type=\"button\" data-mode=\"copied\" aria-pressed=\"false\">One Poisson count, copied twice</button></div><div class=\"v7-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-preset=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"true\">U=.12, V=.80</button><button type=\"button\" data-preset=\"1\" aria-pressed=\"false\">U=.64, V=.08</button><button type=\"button\" data-preset=\"2\" aria-pressed=\"false\">U=.84, V=.84</button></div><picture data-v7-picture><source media=\"(max-width:700px)\" srcset=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-volume7-v1/V48-en-independent-0-mobile.svg\"><img class=\"v7-scene\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-volume7-v1/V48-en-independent-0-desktop.svg\" alt=\"Poisson in each window is not yet independence\" loading=\"eager\"></picture><div class=\"v7-print\"><section><h4>Poisson in each window is not yet independence · 1/2</h4><img src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-volume7-v1/V48.en.page1.svg\" alt=\"Poisson in each window is not yet independence\"><p class=\"v7-print-caption\">The space has two locations a,b and permits multiplicities. Independent counts K_a,K_b are Poisson(1); the copied model sets both counts equal to one Poisson(1) variable K. Marginals and mean measures agree, but the probability of two empty windows is exp(-2) versus exp(-1). Independent uniforms U,V in [0,1) form a common input: two inverse CDFs in the first model, U alone in the second. Shaded probabilities are exact continuous-input areas. Buttons specify illustrative inputs, not simulations. This two-location example does not replace the general PRM construction or scattering proof.</p></section><section><h4>Poisson in each window is not yet independence · 2/2</h4><img src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-volume7-v1/V48.en.page2.svg\" alt=\"Poisson in each window is not yet independence\"><p class=\"v7-print-caption\">The space has two locations a,b and permits multiplicities. Independent counts K_a,K_b are Poisson(1); the copied model sets both counts equal to one Poisson(1) variable K. Marginals and mean measures agree, but the probability of two empty windows is exp(-2) versus exp(-1). Independent uniforms U,V in [0,1) form a common input: two inverse CDFs in the first model, U alone in the second. Shaded probabilities are exact continuous-input areas. Buttons specify illustrative inputs, not simulations. This two-location example does not replace the general PRM construction or scattering proof.</p></section></div><output data-v7-result aria-live=\"polite\">Both empty: exp(-2)≈0.1353; each empty marginal: exp(-1).</output><details><summary>Assumptions and diagram limits</summary><p>The space has two locations a,b and permits multiplicities. Independent counts K_a,K_b are Poisson(1); the copied model sets both counts equal to one Poisson(1) variable K. Marginals and mean measures agree, but the probability of two empty windows is exp(-2) versus exp(-1). Independent uniforms U,V in [0,1) form a common input: two inverse CDFs in the first model, U alone in the second. Shaded probabilities are exact continuous-input areas. Buttons specify illustrative inputs, not simulations. This two-location example does not replace the general PRM construction or scattering proof.</p></details><figcaption>An exact finite model reveals the mechanism; full theorems and proofs remain in the text.</figcaption><nav><a href=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-volume7-v1/V48.en.svg\">SVG</a><a href=\"/print/figures/V48.en.html\">Static print</a></nav></figure>",
